msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:10
msgid ""
"[RFC 7234](http://httpwg.org/specs/rfc7234.html) compliant HTTP caching "
"for native Node.js HTTP/HTTPS requests. Caching works out of the box in "
"memory or is easily pluggable with a wide range of storage adapters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:12
msgid ""
"**Note:** This is a low level wrapper around the core HTTP modules, it's "
"not a high level request library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:14
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:16
msgid "Only stores cacheable responses as defined by RFC 7234"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:17
msgid "Fresh cache entries are served directly from cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:18
msgid ""
"Stale cache entries are revalidated with `If-None-Match`/`If-Modified-"
"Since` headers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:19
msgid "304 responses from revalidation requests use cached body"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:20
msgid "Updates `Age` header on cached responses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:21
msgid "Can completely bypass cache on a per request basis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:22
msgid "In memory cache by default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:23
msgid ""
"Official support for Redis, MongoDB, SQLite, PostgreSQL and MySQL storage"
" adapters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:24
msgid "Easily plug in your own or third-party storage adapters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:25
msgid ""
"If DB connection fails, cache is automatically bypassed ([disabled by "
"default](#optsautomaticfailover))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:26
msgid "Adds cache support to any existing HTTP code with minimal changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:27
msgid ""
"Uses [http-cache-semantics](https://github.com/pornel/http-cache-"
"semantics) internally for HTTP RFC 7234 compliance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:29
msgid "Install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:35
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:56
msgid "Storage Adapters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:58
msgid ""
"`cacheable-request` uses [Keyv](https://github.com/lukechilds/keyv) to "
"support a wide range of storage adapters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:60
msgid ""
"For example, to use Redis as a cache backend, you just need to install "
"the official Redis Keyv storage adapter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:66
msgid "And then you can pass `CacheableRequest` your connection string:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:72
msgid ""
"[View all official Keyv storage "
"adapters.](https://github.com/lukechilds/keyv#official-storage-adapters)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:74
msgid ""
"Keyv also supports anything that follows the Map API so it's easy to "
"write your own storage adapter or use a third-party solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:76
msgid "e.g The following are all valid storage adapters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:89
msgid ""
"View the [Keyv docs](https://github.com/lukechilds/keyv) for more "
"information on how to use storage adapters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:91
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:93
msgid "new cacheableRequest(request, [storageAdapter])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:95
msgid "Returns the provided request function wrapped with cache support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:97
msgid "request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:99
#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:147
msgid "Type: `function`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:101
msgid ""
"Request function to wrap with cache support. Should be "
"[`http.request`](https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_http_request_options_callback)"
" or a similar API compatible request function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:103
msgid "storageAdapter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:105
msgid "Type: `Keyv storage adapter`<br> Default: `new Map()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:108
msgid ""
"A [Keyv](https://github.com/lukechilds/keyv) storage adapter instance, or"
" connection string if using with an official Keyv storage adapter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:110
msgid "Instance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:112
msgid "cacheableRequest(opts, [cb])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:114
msgid "Returns an event emitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:116
msgid "opts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:118
msgid "Type: `object`, `string`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:120
msgid "Any of the default request functions options plus:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:122
msgid "opts.cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:124
msgid "Type: `boolean`<br> Default: `true`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:127
msgid ""
"If the cache should be used. Setting this to false will completely bypass"
" the cache for the current request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:129
msgid "opts.strictTtl"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:131
#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:140
msgid "Type: `boolean`<br> Default: `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:134
msgid ""
"If set to `false`, after a cached resource's TTL expires it is kept in "
"the cache and will be revalidated on the next request with `If-None-Match"
"`/`If-Modified-Since` headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:136
msgid ""
"If set to `true` once a cached resource has expired it is deleted and "
"will have to be re-requested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:138
msgid "opts.automaticFailover"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:143
msgid ""
"When set to `true`, if the DB connection fails we will automatically "
"fallback to a network request. DB errors will still be emitted to notify "
"you of the problem even though the request callback may succeed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:145
msgid "cb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:149
msgid "The callback function which will receive the response as an argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:151
msgid ""
"The response can be either a [Node.js HTTP response "
"stream](https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_class_http_incomingmessage)"
" or a [responselike object](https://github.com/lukechilds/responselike). "
"The response will also have a `fromCache` property set with a boolean "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:153
msgid ".on('request', request)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:155
msgid "`request` event to get the request object of the request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:157
msgid ""
"**Note:** This event will only fire if an HTTP request is actually made, "
"not when a response is retrieved from cache. However, you should always "
"handle the `request` event to end the request and handle any potential "
"request errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:159
msgid ".on('response', response)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:161
msgid ""
"`response` event to get the response object from the HTTP request or "
"cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:163
msgid ".on('error', error)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:165
msgid "`error` event emitted in case of an error with the cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:167
msgid ""
"Errors emitted here will be an instance of "
"`CacheableRequest.RequestError` or `CacheableRequest.CacheError`. You "
"will only ever receive a `RequestError` if the request function throws "
"(normally caused by invalid user input). Normal request errors should be "
"handled inside the `request` event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:169
msgid ""
"To properly handle all error scenarios you should use the following "
"pattern:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cacheable-request_README.md:186
msgid ""
"**Note:** Database connection errors are emitted here, however "
"`cacheable-request` will attempt to re-request the resource and bypass "
"the cache on a connection error. Therefore a database connection error "
"doesn't necessarily mean the request won't be fulfilled."
msgstr ""

